  <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>NIE: Real Decreto 557/2011 (Immigration Regulation), article 206; fee via form 790, code 012 (Ministerio del Interior).</li>
    <li>7% transfer tax and 1.2% AJD in Andalusia: Ley 5/2021 de Tributos Cedidos de la Comunidad Autónoma de Andalucía (BOJA, 22 October 2021). 10% VAT on new homes: Ley 37/1992 (VAT Act), article 91.</li>
    <li>Arras: Código Civil, article 1454.</li>
    <li>Community debts: Ley 49/1960 de Propiedad Horizontal, article 9.1.e. IBI attaches to the property: Real Decreto Legislativo 2/2004 (Local Finance Act), article 64.</li>
    <li>Plusvalía and the buyer as substitute for a non-resident seller: Real Decreto Legislativo 2/2004, article 106.2.</li>
    <li>3% withholding for a non-resident seller: Real Decreto Legislativo 5/2004 (Non-Resident Income Tax Act), article 25.2; form 211 of the Agencia Tributaria.</li>
    <li>Cash payment limit: Ley 7/2012, article 7, as amended by Ley 11/2021.</li>
    <li>Energy certificate: Real Decreto 390/2021.</li>
    <li>Building on rural land and AFO in Andalusia: Ley 7/2021 de Impulso para la Sostenibilidad del Territorio de Andalucía (LISTA) and Decreto 550/2022 (implementing regulation).</li>
    <li>Nota simple: Colegio de Registradores (registradores.org). Cadastre: Sede Electrónica del Catastro.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note">Checked on 5 November 2026. This guide gives general information and is not legal, tax or financial advice. Rules and rates can change; have your purchase handled by an independent lawyer and ask a tax adviser about your own situation.</p>
</Guide>
